[검색 발췌 요지 — Reuters, 트레이더 소식통 4명]
- China is set to resume refined fuel exports for October after a short pause over its Golden Week holiday.
- NDRC and the Ministry of Commerce did not immediately respond to requests for comment (공식 확인 없음).
- Two industry sources put October approvals for gasoline, diesel and jet fuel at about 3.7 million metric tons combined, vs slightly more than 4 million tons expected in September.
- Beijing began curbing fuel exports in March ... Controls were relaxed between July and September. Regulators vet shipments month by month.
- Energy Aspects analyst: impact "will be limited as markets remain tight overall and Middle Eastern supplies are still disrupted."

